// Steam discussion post for v1.4.0 -- paste everything below the rule into a
// new Workshop discussion thread. Goes up BEFORE the Workshop upload (promised
// in the Sep 3 reply). Release-notes voice: what changed, by the point it
// answers. No first person, no notes about what was left alone.
//
// Suggested title:
//   1.4.0 before it hits the Workshop: what a bracket means now
//
// One line per paragraph on purpose: Steam preserves newlines, so hard-wrapped
// text breaks mid-sentence. Long form with the reasoning is in
// ADVANCED_SCENARIOS_PLAN.md section 8.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

[b]Running the game's code (UserK, KoObEy)[/b]

The test suite now runs Noita's own cast code alongside the mod and compares what each one pulls out of the wand, spell by spell. Three bugs it found, all fixed:

[list]
[*]Alpha, Gamma and Tau no longer merge into the cast after them. Every cast boundary past a Greek was one spell too far down the wand, and a wand ending in a Greek was tagged "wraps to front" when it does not wrap.
[*]Add Trigger, Add Timer and Add Death Trigger now scan past the modifiers in front of the projectile and bracket the whole group. "Add Trigger, Damage Plus, Spark Bolt, Bomb" was drawn as two casts; it is one.
[*]A spell with 0 charges at the end of a wand no longer reports a wrap.
[/list]

[b]What a bracket means (KoObEy #4)[/b]

A bracket now means exactly one thing:

[quote]A bracket holds exactly the spells the game took out of the wand while casting the first spell in the bracket. A spell that gets re-cast by reference (Alpha, Omega, ...) was never taken out, so it is never inside a bracket -- the panel names it as a copy instead.[/quote]

What follows from it: a trigger's payload sits inside the trigger, because the trigger pulls it out of the wand even though it fires later. Divide By and Add Trigger sit in front of what they pull. Greeks get no bracket around the spell they copy. Reset's bracket is the whole rest of the wand.

Open for argument before it reaches the Workshop, since everything else hangs off it.

[b]Wands the mod can't read (KoObEy #1)[/b]

Every spell now carries a confidence rating. A wand holding something the mod cannot follow exactly -- a Greek, a Requirement spell, a random draw, an unknown modded spell -- draws no brackets at all, tags itself "? uncertain", and names the spell responsible in the panel. A blank row beats a confident wrong one. A setting draws them anyway for anyone who wants the approximation.

Two exceptions. Add Trigger keeps its brackets, now that it can be followed exactly. Divide By keeps them in front of a plain projectile, and drops them in front of a multicast, trigger or modifier, where the game re-runs the divided spell and pulls fresh spells each time.

[b]0 charges (KoObEy #3)[/b]

Depleted spells are handled the way the game handles them: skipped, with the next spell drawn in their place. If the wand runs out during that skip the draw is lost and nothing wraps. "Greek Wands: Keep Depleted Spells" no longer does anything and will be removed next release.

[b]Modded spells (Night, KoObEy #2)[/b]

Modded spells were being treated as projectiles, which is why one cast could draw as several on a modded wand. The mod now reads the game's live spell list, which includes everything other mods add, so modded modifiers and multicasts group properly. How many spells a modded spell pulls is still unknown, so those wands are marked uncertain rather than guessed at.

[b]Mana (KoObEy #5)[/b]

Each cast's cost is shown and compared against the wand's max mana, with a warning on a cast that can never afford itself.

[b]Where it is[/b]

1.4.0 is on GitHub now, ahead of the Workshop update. Reports of spell mods to test against are welcome.
